  "body": "Closeout for the 2026-06-15 og-strategist session (entered via /og-claim-seat -> redirected to orient+operate on the already-staffed seat; the strategist seat is staffed, this session occupied it). Theme: a single Director-raised friction -- 'the handoff between seats needs a please-check-for-memos human command' -- carried from question to a working, ratified, live-demonstrated capability in one session. ON MAIN (ratified-by-merge under Director direction; commits 59c387c + 644b6ef, author og-strategist / committer Scott): (1) seat-inbox-notification doorbell convention -- proposals/seat-inbox-notification-doorbell.md + decisions/proposal-seat-inbox-notification-doorbell.md; transport-neutral semantic, Claude Code channels recorded as ONE reference transport bounded by four gates (vendor/research-preview/terminal-CLI-only/org-policy), promotion HELD under #8; no charter bump. (2) Path A findings -- memos/2026-06-15-1145 (channels enabled+working in VS Code integrated terminal under a personal Max account; the recipe + every gotcha). (3) Path B PoC -- channels/ package: transport-NEUTRAL doorbell-core.js (watches memos/, read-state, pointer-not-payload -- body never read) + thin Claude Code channel adapter + .mcp.json; built by og-implementer (memos/2026-06-15-1530), strategist-re-verified (5/5 tests + core reviewed), three returned pattern-shape questions resolved (memos/2026-06-15-1600: vendor-neutral transport = YES scope; memodef self-declaration = defer; mark_read persistence = per-session sufficient for warm-standby). C1 LIVE-CONFIRMED this session: a throwaway memo filed from this seat rang the og-implementer-side memo-watch session ('<- memo-watch: New memo filed to og-strategist...') which read + acted on it, with NO human 'check for memos'; pointer-not-payload held in the wild (addressing+path delivered, body never forwarded); and when the rung session proposed deleting the throwaway, the destructive op still hit the permission gate -- layered defense (content-is-data at the transport + bounded authority + permission gate at the action) demonstrated. Throwaway probe deleted; tree clean. OPEN / NEXT: (a) vendor-neutral transport (poll/file-watch reusing doorbell-core unchanged, runtime-agnostic sink, no Anthropic dependency) -- AUTHORIZED, queued for a staffed og-implementer session; landing it satisfies conformance #3 and EARNS the recommended_patterns.general promotion. (b) Director-side: ogframework.com publishing + folding channels/ into the OG distribution kit (parameterized by OG_MEMOS_DIR) + composing with run_seat()/launcher so a bound seat auto-gets its doorbell -- the 'use it in other orgs' roadmap (each step gated: validation / ratification / implementer-execution). (c) Pre-existing untracked items NOT swept by this session: implementer 1530 handback memo + seat-application 2026-06-14-1500 + prior closeouts (2026-05-29-2000, 2026-06-04-1400) remain untracked; .wrangler/ + two modified transcripts untouched. (d) Not pushed -- commits are local on main; push to ogframework/og is the Director's publish step. Bounded authority held throughout: strategist drafted/resolved/scoped + re-verified a peer deliverable; implementer built; Director ratified-by-merge; no seat merged or pushed.",
